{
  "challenges": [
    {
      "publicId": "chal_coding_gcn_142",
      "name": "consistent-hash-ring",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Route restaurants with a consistent hash ring",
      "description": "The gateway sends each restaurant's requests to one courier-matcher instance, which keeps that restaurant's prep-time model in memory. The first router used `hash(restaurant) % instances`: scaling from 4 to 5 instances sent most restaurants to a cold instance and the database took the load. The editor holds the hash ring (`main.go`) with key blocks missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that: each instance gets `vnodes` points on the ring (the file's `hash` of `<instance>#<i>`), kept sorted; `Remove` takes an instance's points off; and `Get` returns the owner of the first point at or after the key's hash, skipping instances that are down and wrapping past the end of the ring. Run assigns 10,000 restaurants before and after a change (add, remove, down) and counts how many moved.",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "outcomes": [
        "traffic-control"
      ],
      "points": 40,
      "hints": [
        "Picture the ring as a sorted list of numbers: which point owns a key whose hash is larger than every point, and what must happen to the list after you append new points?",
        "Look at `sort.Search` (it returns the first index where the condition holds, or len when none does), `sort.Slice`, the modulo of an index by the number of points, and filtering a slice in place.",
        "A cache-shard router with the same shape: 100 points per Redis shard from `fnv(shard + \"#\" + i)`, `i := sort.Search(len(points), func(j int) bool { return points[j] >= fnv(key) })`, then `for n := 0; n < len(points); n++ { s := owner[points[(i+n)%len(points)]]; if healthy[s] { return s } }`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "go",
        "filePath": "main.go",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "10,000 restaurants spread evenly over 4 instances (160 virtual nodes each)",
          "input": {
            "upstreams": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-3",
              "matcher-4"
            ],
            "vnodes": 160,
            "keys": 10000
          },
          "expected": {
            "before": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
            "after": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
            "moved": 0
          },
          "hidden": false,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "Adding a 5th instance moves only about a fifth of the restaurants",
          "input": {
            "upstreams": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-3",
              "matcher-4"
            ],
            "vnodes": 160,
            "keys": 10000,
            "add": "matcher-5"
          },
          "expected": {
            "before": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
            "after": {
              "matcher-1": 1841,
              "matcher-2": 2056,
              "matcher-3": 2008,
              "matcher-4": 1951,
              "matcher-5": 2144
            },
            "moved": 2144
          },
          "hidden": false,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "When matcher-3 is down, only its restaurants move, to the other three",
          "input": {
            "upstreams": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-3",
              "matcher-4"
            ],
            "vnodes": 160,
            "keys": 10000,
            "down": [
              "matcher-3"
            ]
          },
          "expected": {
            "before": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
            "after": {
              "matcher-1": 3433,
              "matcher-2": 3418,
              "matcher-4": 3149
            },
            "moved": 2551
          },
          "hidden": false,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "Removing matcher-2 for good moves only matcher-2's restaurants",
          "input": {
            "upstreams": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-3",
              "matcher-4"
            ],
            "vnodes": 160,
            "keys": 10000,
            "remove": "matcher-2"
          },
          "expected": {
            "before": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
            "after": {
              "matcher-1": 3300,
              "matcher-3": 3537,
              "matcher-4": 3163
            },
            "moved": 2625
          },
          "hidden": true,
          "score": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "With three instances down, every restaurant still gets the one that is up",
          "input": {
            "upstreams": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-3",
              "matcher-4"
            ],
            "vnodes": 160,
            "keys": 10000,
            "down": [
              "matcher-1",
              "matcher-2",
              "matcher-4"
            ]
          },
          "expected": {
            "before": {
              "matcher-1": 2576,
              "matcher-2": 2625,
              "matcher-3": 2551,
              "matcher-4": 2248
            },
